      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Let $S=\\{-2,-4,-6,-8\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(-2)=12,\\,f(-4)=12,\\,f(-6)=3,\\,f(-8)=-5.\n$$\n\nCompute ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$ {{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nThe outputs are $12,$ $12,$ $3,$ and $-5,$ so the maximum output value is $12.$ This maximum occurs at both $x=-2$ and $x=-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=12\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=\\{-2,-4\\}.\n$$",
